Eldaya held the position for sixteen years until her death in . She was Beryl Marle's successor and Alvera Ramosanya's predecessor., Chapter 24 The White Tower}}

She was not weak but not strong either. She left Tower affairs to the Hall as long as she was able to manage her own manipulations elsewhere, which she did quite a lot.

Category:Historical people Category:High Ranking Aes Sedai Category:Channelers Category:Character not mentioned in books Category:Aes Sedai

Ishara Nawan was an Aes Sedai of the Blue Ajah who was raised to the Amyrlin Seat in the year ., Ishara Nawan}}

Ishara's name could indicate Andoran origin (see Ishara Casalain).

Ishara held the position for thirty-five years until her death in . She was Nirelle Coidevwin's successor and Cerilla Marodred's predecessor., Chapter 24 The White Tower}}

Ishara was a strong and influential Amyrlin. She continued the policies of her predecessors but in a modified way, because she involved directly the White Tower in fewer wars. She gained considerable influence but also entangled the Aes Sedai in several dangerous situations that came to a head only after her death.

Kiam Lopiang was an Aes Sedai who lived at the time of the formation of the White Tower., Kiam Lopiang}}

She is the only woman not named as being part of the group that met in to discuss the building of a new city to become the centre for all Aes Sedai., Chapter 9, Formation of the White Tower}}

In Kiam was recorded as being one of seven women providing assistance and council to Elisane Tishar, the first Amyrlin Seat., Chapter 9, Formation of the White Tower}} This is strong evidence that she and her six colleagues represent the founding Aes Sedai who chartered the seven Ajah sisterhoods that would come to define Aes Sedai power and influence. She would have been an Ajah Head. Note that the Hall of the Tower did not yet exist, but would become established by .

